        "original_id": "b00f59e1-b332-5188-8aa1-c93263cb8de8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Prince, Dresti\n- Groups: The Revolution\n- Albums: Purple Rain\n- Songs: I Would Die 4 U\n- Films: Purple Rain\n- Stage names: Space Cowboy\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, Prince released the studio album Purple Rain, his sixth album, as the soundtrack to the 1984 film Purple Rain.\n- In 1984, Purple Rain was the first Prince album to feature his band The Revolution.\n- In 1984, \"I Would Die 4 U\" was a song by Prince and The Revolution on the album Purple Rain.\n- In the United States, \"I Would Die 4 U\" was the fourth single released from Prince and The Revolution's 1984 album Purple Rain.\n- To date, Purple Rain has sold over 25 million copies worldwide.\n- To date, Purple Rain is the third-best-selling soundtrack album of all time.\n- In 2002, Dresti changed his stage name to Space Cowboy.\n- In 2002, Space Cowboy recorded a cover of Prince's song \"I Would Die 4 U.\"",
